The `allowed-client` pod has the label `role=allowed`.

The policy currently denies all ingress. I need to patch `default-deny-ingress` to include an ingress rule that allows traffic from pods matching `role=allowed` to the server pods (which are selected by `{}` in the existing policy, meaning all of them).

The change will be:
1.  Keep `podSelector: {}` (to affect all server pods).
2.  Keep `policyTypes: [Ingress]`.
3.  Add an `ingress` rule that selects pods with `role=allowed` as the source.

The structure of the patch needs to add the ingress rule.

```json
{
  "spec": {
    "podSelector": {},
    "policyTypes": ["Ingress"],
    "ingress": [
      {
        "from": [
          {
            "podSelector": {
              "matchLabels": {
                "role": "allowed"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
